==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From [[:w:Tuxedo Park, New York|Tuxedo Park, New York]], USA, where the fashion is often said to have originated, the village in turn likely from an {{etyl|alg|en}} language ({{etyl|umu|en}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{enPR|tŭksē'dō}}, {{IPA|/tʌkˈsidoʊ/|lang=en}}
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/tʌkˈsiːdəʊ/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|iːdəʊ|lang=en}}

===Noun===
[[Image:Men in black tie.jpg|thumb|right|Three men in tuxedos]]
{{en-noun|tuxedos|tuxedoes}}

# A typically [[black]] [[formal]] [[jacket]] worn by men.
# The entire [[suit]] complementing and including this jacket.

